{"parentUuid":"cf550024-c675-4c6e-9b7d-b7b4339be633","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cc4dbf1e-79de-4dba-bef6-7dc85562f73f","agentId":"a13f3ca3e19263a03","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016wzE9nLz9ufgr6fE9drww3","type":"tool_result","content":"commit c50f90d41f1cd26cb750812c98e0d6adb1093ecd\nAuthor: John D'Angelo <dangelo.john@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Oct 14 12:53:01 2026 -0400\n\n    Fix CSS comment-closing typo that silently dropped the whole foundation :root block in real browsers\n    \n    The typography pass (ed31772) wrote \"--space-*/--fam-*\" inside a prose\n    comment; the literal \"*/\" there closed the comment early, so every real\n    CSS parser (verified via headless Edge CDP, not just the repo's regex-\n    based checks) read the rest of that comment's prose as garbage CSS and\n    discarded the entire :root { ... } foundation block through its closing\n    brace -- --bg, --ink, --sans, --mono, --fs-*, --fw-*, --accent, --sev-*\n    all undefined. Under the OS/browser's light preference this was masked\n    by the separate, well-formed `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light)`\n    block; under dark preference (the default, no data-theme set) the page\n    fell back to transparent background, Times New Roman, 16px, weight 400\n    -- this is the \"visible difference\" from before the pass. Confirmed via\n    a two-server A/B (this commit vs b87ecfe, the true last pre-pass commit)\n    rendered at 768x1024 under both emulated color schemes: after the fix,\n    body background, --bg resolution, hero/heading font-family/weight/size\n    and chip styling are now identical between the two again.\n    \n    One character fixed (space inserted: \"--space-* / --fam-*\"). Previous\n    commit's font-weight 300 restoration on hero/display elements stands.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n cuore/web/static/cuore.css | 2 +-\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\n---diff---\ncommit c50f90d41f1cd26cb750812c98e0d6adb1093ecd\nAuthor: John D'Angelo <dangelo.john@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Oct 14 12:53:01 2026 -0400\n\n    Fix CSS comment-closing typo that silently dropped the whole foundation :root block in real browsers\n    \n    The typography pass (ed31772) wrote \"--space-*/--fam-*\" inside a prose\n    comment; the literal \"*/\" there closed the comment early, so every real\n    CSS parser (verified via headless Edge CDP, not just the repo's regex-\n    based checks) read the rest of that comment's prose as garbage CSS and\n    discarded the entire :root { ... } foundation block through its closing\n    brace -- --bg, --ink, --sans, --mono, --fs-*, --fw-*, --accent, --sev-*\n    all undefined. Under the OS/browser's light preference this was masked\n    by the separate, well-formed `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light)`\n    block; under dark preference (the default, no data-theme set) the page\n    fell back to transparent background, Times New Roman, 16px, weight 400\n    -- this is the \"visible difference\" from before the pass. Confirmed via\n    a two-server A/B (this commit vs b87ecfe, the true last pre-pass commit)\n    rendered at 768x1024 under both emulated color schemes: after the fix,\n    body background, --bg resolution, hero/heading font-family/weight/size\n    and chip styling are now identical between the two again.\n    \n    One character fixed (space inserted: \"--space-* / --fam-*\"). Previous\n    commit's font-weight 300 restoration on hero/display elements stands.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/cuore/web/static/cuore.css b/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\nindex e79210e..2df6abf 100644\n--- a/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\n+++ b/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\n@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@\n  * the identical set of values -- that pair is a mechanism, not a duplicate).\n  * Every later \"additive pass\" in this file used to redeclare its own bare\n  * :root with a handful of overriding values (true-black bg/surface/ink,\n- * then a lone --ink-3, plus --space-*/--fam-* in their own blocks) -- that\n+ * then a lone --ink-3, plus --space-* / --fam-* in their own blocks) -- that\n  * is exactly R2's \"colour tokens declared 3 times on :root\" and \"body\n  * font-size declared 4 times\" symptom. All of that is merged in here, at\n  * its final (last-cascade-wins) value, so there is now exactly one place","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d2af40a1-3f32-4f7e-bdc3-ca5523e7e04e","timestamp":"2026-10-14T17:15:32.469Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"commit c50f90d41f1cd26cb750812c98e0d6adb1093ecd\nAuthor: John D'Angelo <dangelo.john@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Oct 14 12:53:01 2026 -0400\n\n    Fix CSS comment-closing typo that silently dropped the whole foundation :root block in real browsers\n    \n    The typography pass (ed31772) wrote \"--space-*/--fam-*\" inside a prose\n    comment; the literal \"*/\" there closed the comment early, so every real\n    CSS parser (verified via headless Edge CDP, not just the repo's regex-\n    based checks) read the rest of that comment's prose as garbage CSS and\n    discarded the entire :root { ... } foundation block through its closing\n    brace -- --bg, --ink, --sans, --mono, --fs-*, --fw-*, --accent, --sev-*\n    all undefined. Under the OS/browser's light preference this was masked\n    by the separate, well-formed `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light)`\n    block; under dark preference (the default, no data-theme set) the page\n    fell back to transparent background, Times New Roman, 16px, weight 400\n    -- this is the \"visible difference\" from before the pass. Confirmed via\n    a two-server A/B (this commit vs b87ecfe, the true last pre-pass commit)\n    rendered at 768x1024 under both emulated color schemes: after the fix,\n    body background, --bg resolution, hero/heading font-family/weight/size\n    and chip styling are now identical between the two again.\n    \n    One character fixed (space inserted: \"--space-* / --fam-*\"). Previous\n    commit's font-weight 300 restoration on hero/display elements stands.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n cuore/web/static/cuore.css | 2 +-\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\n---diff---\ncommit c50f90d41f1cd26cb750812c98e0d6adb1093ecd\nAuthor: John D'Angelo <dangelo.john@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Oct 14 12:53:01 2026 -0400\n\n    Fix CSS comment-closing typo that silently dropped the whole foundation :root block in real browsers\n    \n    The typography pass (ed31772) wrote \"--space-*/--fam-*\" inside a prose\n    comment; the literal \"*/\" there closed the comment early, so every real\n    CSS parser (verified via headless Edge CDP, not just the repo's regex-\n    based checks) read the rest of that comment's prose as garbage CSS and\n    discarded the entire :root { ... } foundation block through its closing\n    brace -- --bg, --ink, --sans, --mono, --fs-*, --fw-*, --accent, --sev-*\n    all undefined. Under the OS/browser's light preference this was masked\n    by the separate, well-formed `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light)`\n    block; under dark preference (the default, no data-theme set) the page\n    fell back to transparent background, Times New Roman, 16px, weight 400\n    -- this is the \"visible difference\" from before the pass. Confirmed via\n    a two-server A/B (this commit vs b87ecfe, the true last pre-pass commit)\n    rendered at 768x1024 under both emulated color schemes: after the fix,\n    body background, --bg resolution, hero/heading font-family/weight/size\n    and chip styling are now identical between the two again.\n    \n    One character fixed (space inserted: \"--space-* / --fam-*\"). Previous\n    commit's font-weight 300 restoration on hero/display elements stands.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/cuore/web/static/cuore.css b/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\nindex e79210e..2df6abf 100644\n--- a/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\n+++ b/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\n@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@\n  * the identical set of values -- that pair is a mechanism, not a duplicate).\n  * Every later \"additive pass\" in this file used to redeclare its own bare\n  * :root with a handful of overriding values (true-black bg/surface/ink,\n- * then a lone --ink-3, plus --space-*/--fam-* in their own blocks) -- that\n+ * then a lone --ink-3, plus --space-* / --fam-* in their own blocks) -- that\n  * is exactly R2's \"colour tokens declared 3 times on :root\" and \"body\n  * font-size declared 4 times\" symptom. All of that is merged in here, at\n  * its final (last-cascade-wins) value, so there is now exactly one place","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e6507fa6-67ed-42ae-ada0-e8b78ba0f5c1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cf550024-c675-4c6e-9b7d-b7b4339be633","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
