{"parentUuid":"295e3537-b48a-4eed-9624-eca52116005e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a13f3ca3e19263a03","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2WN9ASbYS3rwMFb32Jj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xe1WK2qcu4nQVRFudbPChY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git diff --stat cuore/web/static/cuore.css; echo \"---\"; git diff cuore/web/static/cuore.css | head -150","description":"Show uncommitted cuore.css diff"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2420,"cache_read_input_tokens":89691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2420,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Xe1WK2qcu4nQVRFudbPChY":{"command":"cd /c/Users/User/mcp-servers && git diff --stat cuore/web/static/cuore.css; echo \"---\"; git diff cuore/web/static/cuore.css | head -150","description":"Show uncommitted cuore.css diff"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01Xe1WK2qcu4nQVRFudbPChY":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cca87db5-8ce3-4615-9219-3b3a6e96a7a0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg2WN8YzPUEjJRDfriJfg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"626bf151-e650-4c45-8a8b-a59df06b3db7","timestamp":"2026-10-14T17:15:36.422Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"626bf151-e650-4c45-8a8b-a59df06b3db7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cc4dbf1e-79de-4dba-bef6-7dc85562f73f","agentId":"a13f3ca3e19263a03","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xe1WK2qcu4nQVRFudbPChY","type":"tool_result","content":" cuore/web/static/cuore.css | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n---\ndiff --git a/cuore/web/static/cuore.css b/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\nindex 2df6abf..416f76d 100644\n--- a/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\n+++ b/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\n@@ -193,8 +193,30 @@\n  * bleed (job.css's sticky .step-nav) adds a couple more -- neither is a\n  * real layout bug a mechanic would ever see (nothing visible moves),\n  * but both make the automated scrollWidth check fail, so the page itself\n- * never grows a horizontal scrollbar regardless. */\n-html, body { overflow-x: hidden; }\n+ * never grows a horizontal scrollbar regardless.\n+ * Review 7, 2026-10-14: this used to read `html, body { overflow-x:\n+ * hidden; }`. Confirmed live (real CDP measurement, scrolling\n+ * document.documentElement.scrollTop and watching .vline's own\n+ * getBoundingClientRect) that putting `overflow-x: hidden` on BODY too\n+ * silently breaks every `position: sticky` element on every page --\n+ * CSS's own overflow-x/overflow-y interaction rule forces an element's\n+ * *computed* overflow-y to `auto` whenever its overflow-x is non-visible\n+ * and overflow-y was left at the default `visible`, and that alone makes\n+ * BODY a scroll container by spec, even though body never actually\n+ * overflows itself (it has no constrained height) and\n+ * `document.scrollingElement` stays `html` throughout. .vline/.vbar/\n+ * .flow-bar's nearest *scroll-container* ancestor resolves to that inert\n+ * body box instead of the one that's actually scrolling, so they never\n+ * stick -- confirmed: .vline's rect moved in lock-step with\n+ * document.documentElement.scrollTop (not pinned at top:0) at every\n+ * width tested. HTML alone is where the real document scroll lives\n+ * (`document.scrollingElement === document.documentElement` here), so\n+ * it alone gets the clip; leaving BODY's overflow-x at its default\n+ * `visible` keeps BODY out of the scroll-container reckoning entirely,\n+ * which restores every sticky element without reopening the horizontal-\n+ * scroll gap this rule exists for (nothing inside BODY can scroll\n+ * sideways on its own once HTML itself cannot). */\n+html { overflow-x: hidden; }\n \n html {\n   font-size: 100%; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; text-size-adjust: 100%;\n@@ -1560,9 +1582,18 @@ h2, .section-h, .step-title {\n   text-transform: uppercase;\n }\n @keyframes intro-in { to { opacity: 1; } }\n+/* Review 7, 2026-10-14: pointer-events:none only fired at 100% (fully\n+ * invisible), so the still-visible fade-out stretch (72%-100%) kept\n+ * catching the very first real tap of a session -- confirmed on the\n+ * Modifications detail page's own Record button (the same root cause\n+ * m_base.html's .m-body override already fixes for the mobile app).\n+ * Moving pointer-events:none to the start of that same stretch here, in\n+ * the shared desktop rule every base.html page uses, fixes it everywhere\n+ * at once rather than per-page. */\n @keyframes intro-fade {\n   0% { opacity: 1; }\n   72% { opacity: 1; }\n+  72.01% { pointer-events: none; }\n   100% { opacity: 0; visibility: hidden; pointer-events: none; }\n }\n /* Shown once per browser session -- _intro.html's inline script adds this","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ed5beae8-ecfd-4ff9-969e-0a94d1bab127","timestamp":"2026-10-14T17:15:37.045Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":" cuore/web/static/cuore.css | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n---\ndiff --git a/cuore/web/static/cuore.css b/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\nindex 2df6abf..416f76d 100644\n--- a/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\n+++ b/cuore/web/static/cuore.css\n@@ -193,8 +193,30 @@\n  * bleed (job.css's sticky .step-nav) adds a couple more -- neither is a\n  * real layout bug a mechanic would ever see (nothing visible moves),\n  * but both make the automated scrollWidth check fail, so the page itself\n- * never grows a horizontal scrollbar regardless. */\n-html, body { overflow-x: hidden; }\n+ * never grows a horizontal scrollbar regardless.\n+ * Review 7, 2026-10-14: this used to read `html, body { overflow-x:\n+ * hidden; }`. Confirmed live (real CDP measurement, scrolling\n+ * document.documentElement.scrollTop and watching .vline's own\n+ * getBoundingClientRect) that putting `overflow-x: hidden` on BODY too\n+ * silently breaks every `position: sticky` element on every page --\n+ * CSS's own overflow-x/overflow-y interaction rule forces an element's\n+ * *computed* overflow-y to `auto` whenever its overflow-x is non-visible\n+ * and overflow-y was left at the default `visible`, and that alone makes\n+ * BODY a scroll container by spec, even though body never actually\n+ * overflows itself (it has no constrained height) and\n+ * `document.scrollingElement` stays `html` throughout. .vline/.vbar/\n+ * .flow-bar's nearest *scroll-container* ancestor resolves to that inert\n+ * body box instead of the one that's actually scrolling, so they never\n+ * stick -- confirmed: .vline's rect moved in lock-step with\n+ * document.documentElement.scrollTop (not pinned at top:0) at every\n+ * width tested. HTML alone is where the real document scroll lives\n+ * (`document.scrollingElement === document.documentElement` here), so\n+ * it alone gets the clip; leaving BODY's overflow-x at its default\n+ * `visible` keeps BODY out of the scroll-container reckoning entirely,\n+ * which restores every sticky element without reopening the horizontal-\n+ * scroll gap this rule exists for (nothing inside BODY can scroll\n+ * sideways on its own once HTML itself cannot). */\n+html { overflow-x: hidden; }\n \n html {\n   font-size: 100%; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; text-size-adjust: 100%;\n@@ -1560,9 +1582,18 @@ h2, .section-h, .step-title {\n   text-transform: uppercase;\n }\n @keyframes intro-in { to { opacity: 1; } }\n+/* Review 7, 2026-10-14: pointer-events:none only fired at 100% (fully\n+ * invisible), so the still-visible fade-out stretch (72%-100%) kept\n+ * catching the very first real tap of a session -- confirmed on the\n+ * Modifications detail page's own Record button (the same root cause\n+ * m_base.html's .m-body override already fixes for the mobile app).\n+ * Moving pointer-events:none to the start of that same stretch here, in\n+ * the shared desktop rule every base.html page uses, fixes it everywhere\n+ * at once rather than per-page. */\n @keyframes intro-fade {\n   0% { opacity: 1; }\n   72% { opacity: 1; }\n+  72.01% { pointer-events: none; }\n   100% { opacity: 0; visibility: hidden; pointer-events: none; }\n }\n /* Shown once per browser session -- _intro.html's inline script adds this","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"cca87db5-8ce3-4615-9219-3b3a6e96a7a0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"626bf151-e650-4c45-8a8b-a59df06b3db7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
